[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2570262847","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101121#issuecomment-2570262847","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101121","id":2570262847,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ZMxk_","user":{"login":"Ikanaut","id":193673221,"node_id":"U_kgDOC4s4BQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/193673221?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ikanaut","html_url":"https://github.com/Ikanaut","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ikanaut/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ikanaut/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ikanaut/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ikanaut/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ikanaut/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ikanaut/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ikanaut/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ikanaut/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ikanaut/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-04T06:26:08Z","updated_at":"2025-01-04T06:26:08Z","body":"I should add that the \"corrupting the project\" part isn't directly related. Godot projects sometimes become corrupted if the computer dies or crashes while saving and/or running the game. I haven't experienced this in a while, so it may be fixed but I can't be sure.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2570262847/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2589974326","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101121#issuecomment-2589974326","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101121","id":2589974326,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6aX982","user":{"login":"Ikanaut","id":193673221,"node_id":"U_kgDOC4s4BQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/193673221?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ikanaut","html_url":"https://github.com/Ikanaut","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ikanaut/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ikanaut/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ikanaut/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ikanaut/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ikanaut/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ikanaut/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ikanaut/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ikanaut/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ikanaut/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-14T13:50:52Z","updated_at":"2025-01-14T13:50:52Z","body":"Since I've submitted this issue, I have started to suspect that it's caused by a memory leak. I read recently that Linux shuts itself off when RAM maxes out and given that the bug begins by slowing the OS down, it seems likely that Godot is leaking memory rapidly and consuming all of the available RAM.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2589974326/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2907949850","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101121#issuecomment-2907949850","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101121","id":2907949850,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6tU8sa","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-25T17:08:58Z","updated_at":"2025-05-25T18:01:24Z","body":"Can't reproduce here on current 3.x:\n\n`Godot Engine v3.7.dev.custom_build [9cf115186] - X11 - 2 monitors - GLES3 - Mesa Intel(R) Graphics (RPL-S) - 13th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-13700T (24 threads)`\n\nLinux Mint 21.1 Cinnamon 64Gb RAM\n\nRAM usage by the app is steady at 46.4Mb for me (in system monitor).\n\nUPDATE:\nAh a clue. Tried it in 3.6 stable and I get some error output:\n`W 0:00:21.269   _render_target_allocate: Cannot create render target larger than maximum hardware supported size of (16384, 16384). Setting size to maximum.\n  <C++ Source>  drivers/gles2/rasterizer_storage_gles2.cpp:5090 @ _render_target_allocate()`\n\nI'll see if I can track down where this is happening.\n\n`Viewport::set_size()` is being called for me with width 23270 height 13089, for a thin window...\nthe gravy thickens... 🤔 \n\nSeems to be something to do with `STRETCH_ASPECT_EXPAND`. Even just a single control seems to get very high width and height if `STRETCH_ASPECT_EXPAND` is set for the application and a you resize it to a thin window.\n\nI'm not entirely sure what this `STRETCH_ASPECT_EXPAND` is meant to do but will experiment.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2907949850/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2908794226","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101121#issuecomment-2908794226","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101121","id":2908794226,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6tYK1y","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-26T07:16:38Z","updated_at":"2025-05-26T07:16:38Z","body":"It may be worth seeing if this also occurs in 4.x BTW, if it does, then the relevant contributors are more likely to be able to address it.\n\nIf I get time I'll look at this more, I can in theory fix, but I don't know how it is _supposed_ to work, which makes it a little harder to come up with a sensible fix.\n\nI suspect just clamping the max viewport size to the largest dimension, and using the desired aspect ratio is the way to go.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2908794226/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]